==Old English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/sweord/|lang=ang}}

===Etymology===
{{proto|gem-pro|swerdan|lang=ang|literally ‘pricking, piercing thing’}} , of uncertain origin, but most likely from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{recons|swer-||‘fester, suppurate’ later ‘pierce, wound’|lang=ine-pro}}, .
Cognate with Old Frisian ''[[swerd]]'', Old Saxon ''[[swerd]]'' (Dutch ''[[zwaard]])'', Old High German ''[[swert]]'' (German ''[[Schwert]]''), Old Norse ''[[sverð]]'' (Danish ''[[sværd]]'', Norwegian ''[[sverd]]'', Swedish ''[[svärd]])''

